Z||000002||Hartz||10-22-2001||08:28 PM||||I'm all for it - but only if Cliff is for it.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>One thing though, it has been my experience that not many Fiero folks are all that interested in quarter mile times.  That's not to say there aren't people out there who are, and it isn't a flame in anyway, it's just kind of an odd observation I have made.<P>Hartz<P>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo<BR>hartzfeld.home.mindspring.com<P>||||reg||14
Z||000003||Fformula88||10-22-2001||08:39 PM||||I wouldn't say they aren't interested... they just don't post about it a lot.  <P>The debate about whether or not to add more forums has gone on a long time here.  Basically, Cliff and I think the majority of members agree that having the small number of forums that are here keeps everthing from becoming too diverse.  Some of the other boards are broken down into 15+ forums, and there is no sense of community anymore as everyone gravitates towards the seperate forums.  I won't get into all the pros and cons here (do a search, there is a lot of stuff on this) but I think the forum is better as a small forum.<P>You have 1/4 times?  Post them here in the General Fiero forum!  I am sure a lot of members will post back with theirs!||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||10-22-2001||08:52 PM||||Don't forget that Cliff pays for everything out of his own pocket and that this forum also consumes his time of which he doesn't to my knowledge get compensated for.<P>I like the forum the way it is. <BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
